From: HakiOS
Subject: [PATCH 0158] sweet fb: sweetfb_scale boot-arg overrides the ADT render choice (60 FPS A/B)

0129 rendered 750x1624 and scaled to the panel (the only configuration ever
measured at 60 presents/s: 0131r p90 58, 0143r2 p90 49), but 0138 made the
path ADT-driven (canvas-width/height = 750x1624 selects it) so a native ADT
could not A/B it without rebuilding the image.

Restore 0129's override on top of 0138:
  sweetfb_scale=2   force the 750x1624 render + 1.5x panel scale
  sweetfb_scale=1   force native 1:1 (same as sweetfb_native=1)
  absent / 0        follow the ADT canvas (current default, native on the
                    shipped ADT)
No default change: the shipped boot-args do not set it. The scaled path was
verified with the 0131 column map and by 0143r2; 750 layout/UX is untested,
so this stays an experiment.
---
diff --git a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp
index 2c8f2ed..135c8e0 100644
--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp
@@ -551,7 +551,16 @@ AppleCLCD::start(IOService *provider)
 	 */
 	uint32_t canvasW = sweet_dt_u32(provider, "canvas-width");
 	uint32_t canvasH = sweet_dt_u32(provider, "canvas-height");
-	if (canvasW == 750 && canvasH == 1624 && !native && fWidth <= 1080 && fHeight <= 2400) {
+	/*
+	 * 0158: 0129's boot-arg override on top of 0138's ADT choice, so the scaled
+	 * path can be A/B'd without rebuilding the ADT: sweetfb_scale=2 forces the
+	 * 750x1624 render, =1 forces native, absent/0 follows canvas-width/height.
+	 */
+	int scaleArg = 0;
+	PE_parse_boot_argn("sweetfb_scale", &scaleArg, sizeof(scaleArg));
+	const bool wantScale = scaleArg == 2 ||
+	    (scaleArg == 0 && canvasW == 750 && canvasH == 1624);
+	if (wantScale && !native && fWidth <= 1080 && fHeight <= 2400) {
 		/* 0129: iPhone X @2x in points, cropped 720x1600 and scaled 1.5x to the panel */
 		fLogicalW = 750;
 		fLogicalH = 1624;
